  "decision": {
    "answer": "SUPPORTS",
    "explanation": "The provided evidence explicitly characterizes the somatic CTCF R377H variant as a loss-of-function mutation that abrogates the tumour suppressive effects of CTCF. The source text (pmid-28319062:f01) states: \"R377H and P378L are loss-of-function mutations which abrogate the tumour suppressive effects of CTCF. These inter-ZF mutations may alter the conserved DNA binding domain structure and prevent normal CTCF function.\" This directly supports the claim that the variant is functionally characterized as a loss-of-function mutation affecting the tumour suppressive effects, likely by altering the conserved DNA binding domain structure. Other modalities (timeline, pathology, drug) are not applicable as no input was supplied, but the molecular evidence is sufficient to support the claim.",
